      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I believe I may have found the origin of both this issue and why the same problem occurs upon entering Sub-State Machines.\nAssuming that the developers are storing a map, table, or some other container that links the hashed name of a state to its actual name when the Avatar is built for later determining the name of a running state in-game using AnimatorStateInfo.fullPathHash, I think they may be incorrectly hashing the names.\nThere is little to no documentation from Unity about this as far as I'm aware, but the hashed value that AnimatorStateInfo.fullPathHash contains is a string containing the path of State Machines to the State (Ex. \"<STATE_MACHINE>.<SUB_STATE_MACHINE>.<STATE>\"), however some online forums mistakenly claimed that it was the name of the Layer and the State (Ex. \"<LAYER>.<STATE>\"). This is only true when there are no Sub-State Machines and the Layer's primary State Machine is named the same as the Layer. \nIt's quite possible the developers saw one of these forum posts, implemented it this way by accident, and it never was noticed or no one cared to fix it. So instead, when the Debug menu fails to find the name of the State, it simply displays the hash value it received from AnimatorStateInfo.fullPathHash.\nDo remember that this is all speculation though, I don't have access to the source code of VRChat after all. I did however manage to replicate this behavior with a few scripts in Unity perfectly as can be seen in the GIF, as well as what happens when the State Machine names are used for correctly hashing the State names instead.\nEDIT: Turns out the Unity Documentation itself is also wrong about this. For the method IsName() within the AnimatorStateInfo class, it says to use the form *Layer.Name* when it actually needs to be using the State Machine names instead.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
    {
      "__v": 0,
      "_id": "5f5d85be3cdb2644ff244be7",
      "author": {
        "_id": "5a4e9aae15d29048e1d04617",
        "alias": "Gunmetal Chinchilla",
        "aliasID": "65ba01d7ed6eefce4cfc6498",
